oor, model confounds) novel insights or predictable outcomes?\n   - Is the inverted-U finding a genuine contribution?\n   - How does this compare to general findings about self-consistency limitations?\n\n2. **Related Work Coverage**:\n   - Only 10 references total. Is this adequate for a venue-level submission?\n   - Missing areas: uncertainty quantification for structured prediction, calibration literature, other test-time scaling methods, selective prediction, conformal prediction for NLP\n   - Are there works on self-consistency limitations that should be cited?\n   - Missing: Jiang et al. on verbalized uncertainty, Lin et al. on teaching models to express uncertainty, Kuhn et al. on semantic uncertainty\n\n3. **Significance and Impact**:\n   - Who benefits from this paper? How large is the potential audience?\n   - Does the paper provide sufficient actionable guidance beyond \"don't use consistency\"?\n   - Is the \"practitioner guidelines\" contribution strong enough given how restrictive the conditions are?\n\n4. **Framing and Narrative**:\n   - Is the negative-result framing convincing?\n   - Does the paper adequately motivate why anyone would expect consistency to work for structured prediction in the first place?\n   - Is the comparison to reasoning tasks (Section 8.2) compelling?\n\n5. **Positioning Gaps**:\n   - Is there a missed opportunity to connect to calibration/selective prediction literature?\n   - Should the paper discuss alternative confidence methods more thoroughly?\n   - Is the paper too narrowly focused on SJ vs FK when the broader question is about any consistency-based approach?\n\n6. **Strengths and Weaknesses**: List top 3 strengths and top 3 weaknesses.\n\n7. **Score**: Provide your preliminary score (1-6) with justification.\n\n8. **Questions for Authors**: List 3-5 questions you would ask.\n\nFormat your review clearly with headers. Be rigorous—negative result papers need strong positioning and thorough literature coverage to justify venue-level acceptance.","uuid":"b628f0ad-a161-4204-98fb-9a267042347f","session_id":"37f786ee-7832-4fe8-ada0-13058d333aba"}
