{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01UdwK6oVaCxhnPQ47ZH3W6Z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Xem1h8SM6RRfD1yKcYYsTs","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/artifacts/evaluation.py"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":17579,"cache_read_input_tokens":42274,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":17579,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01HKfzCDwhxMENhz8xdBgfGN","session_id":"37f786ee-7832-4fe8-ada0-13058d333aba","uuid":"67b4c476-7480-47c3-bd0f-544e68b425eb"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xem1h8SM6RRfD1yKcYYsTs","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Evaluation module for structured self-consistency IE experiments.\n2\t\n3\tProvides strict-match NER/EAE evaluation, per-instance F1 computation,\n4\tcorrelation analysis, and summary report generation.\n5\t\"\"\"\n6\t\n7\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n8\t\n9\timport statistics\n10\tfrom typing import Any\n11\t\n12\tfrom scipy.stats import spearmanr\n13\t\n14\t\n15\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n16\t# NER evaluation (strict match)\n17\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n18\t\n19\tdef entity_strict_match(\n20\t    pred_entities: list[dict],\n21\t    gold_entities: list[dict],\n22\t) -> tuple[int, int, int]:\n23\t    \"\"\"Compute strict entity match counts.\n24\t\n25\t    Strict match requires exact span (start, end) AND exact type.\n26\t\n27\t    Args:\n28\t        pred_entities: Predicted entity dicts with keys text, type, start, end.\n29\t        gold_entities: Gold entity dicts with the same schema.\n30\t\n31\t    Returns:\n32\t        (tp, fp, fn) counts.\n33\t    \"\"\"\n34\t    pred_set = {(e[\"start\"], e[\"end\"], e[\"type\"]) for e in pred_entities}\n35\t    gold_set = {(e[\"start\"], e[\"end\"], e[\"type\"]) for e in gold_entities}\n36\t    tp = len(pred_set & gold_set)\n37\t    fp = len(pred_set - gold_set)\n38\t    fn = len(gold_set - pred_set)\n39\t    return tp, fp, fn\n40\t\n41\t\n42\tdef compute_ner_f1(\n43\t    predictions: list[dict],\n44\t    golds: list[dict],\n45\t) -> dict[str, float]:\n46\t    \"\"\"Compute micro-averaged NER precision, recall, and F1.\n47\t\n48\t    Args:\n49\t        predictions: List of Extraction dicts (one per instance).\n50\t        golds: List of Extraction dicts (one per instance), aligned with predictions.\n51\t\n52\t    Returns:\n53\t        Dict with keys \"precision\", \"recall\", \"f1\".\n54\t    \"\"\"\n55\t    total_tp = total_fp = total_fn = 0\n56\t    for pred, gold in zip(predictions, golds):\n57\t        tp, fp, fn = entity_strict_match(\n58\t            pred.get(\"entities\", []),\n59\t            gold.get(\"entities\", []),\n60\t        )\n61\t        total_tp += tp\n62\t        total_fp += fp\n63\t        total_fn += fn\n64\t    return _prf(total_tp, total_fp, total_fn)\n65\t\n66\t\n67\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n68\t# EAE evaluation (argument match)\n69\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n70\t\n71\tdef _event_argument_tuples(events: list[dict]) -> set[tuple]:\n72\t    \"\"\"Extract (trigger_start, trigger_end, trigger_type, role, arg_start, arg_end) tuples.\"\"\"\n73\t    tuples: set[tuple] = set()\n74\t    for event in events:\n75\t        trigger = event.get(\"trigger\", {})\n76\t        t_start = trigger.get(\"start\")\n77\t        t_end = trigger.get(\"end\")\n78\t        t_type = trigger.get(\"type\")\n79\t        for arg in event.get(\"arguments\", []):\n80\t            tuples.add((t_start, t_end, t_type, arg[\"role\"], arg[\"start\"], arg[\"end\"]))\n81\t    return tuples\n82\t\n83\t\n84\tdef relation_strict_match(\n85\t    pred_relations: list[dict],\n86\t    gold_relations: list[dict],\n87\t) -> tuple[int, int, int]:\n88\t    \"\"\"Strict relation match: (head_start, head_end, tail_start, tail_end, type) must all match.\"\"\"\n89\t    pred_set = {(r[\"head_start\"], r[\"head_end\"], r[\"tail_start\"], r[\"tail_end\"], r[\"type\"]) for r in pred_relations}\n90\t    gold_set = {(r[\"head_start\"], r[\"head_end\"], r[\"tail_start\"], r[\"tail_end\"], r[\"type\"]) for r in gold_relations}\n91\t    tp = len(pred_set & gold_set)\n92\t    fp = len(pred_set - gold_set)\n93\t    fn = len(gold_set - pred_set)\n94\t    return tp, fp, fn\n95\t\n96\t\n97\tdef compute_re_f1(\n98\t    predictions: list[dict],\n99\t    golds: list[dict],\n100\t) -> dict[str, float]:\n101\t    \"\"\"Compute micro-averaged RE precision, recall, and F1.\"\"\"\n102\t    total_tp = total_fp = total_fn = 0\n103\t    for pred, gold in zip(predictions, golds):\n104\t        tp, fp, fn = relation_strict_match(\n105\t            pred.get(\"relations\", []),\n106\t            gold.get(\"relations\", []),\n107\t        )\n108\t        total_tp += tp\n109\t        total_fp += fp\n110\t        total_fn += fn\n111\t    return _prf(total_tp, total_fp, total_fn)\n112\t\n113\t\n114\tdef argument_match(\n115\t    pred_events: list[dict],\n116\t    gold_events: list[dict],\n117\t) -> tuple[int, int, int]:\n118\t    \"\"\"Compute event argument match counts.\n119\t\n120\t    A correct argument requires trigger span match + trigger type match +\n121\t    argument role match + argument span match.\n122\t\n123\t    Args:\n124\t        pred_events: Predicted Event dicts.\n125\t        gold_events: Gold Event dicts.\n126\t\n127\t    Returns:\n128\t        (tp, fp, fn) counts.\n129\t    \"\"\"\n130\t    pred_set = _event_argument_tuples(pred_events)\n131\t    gold_set = _event_argument_tuples(gold_events)\n132\t    tp = len(pred_set & gold_set)\n133\t    fp = len(pred_set - gold_set)\n134\t    fn = len(gold_set - pred_set)\n135\t    return tp, fp, fn\n136\t\n137\t\n138\tdef compute_eae_f1(\n139\t    predictions: list[dict],\n140\t    golds: list[dict],\n141\t) -> dict[str, float]:\n142\t    \"\"\"Compute micro-averaged EAE precision, recall, and F1.\n143\t\n144\t    Args:\n145\t        predictions: List of Extraction dicts (one per instance).\n146\t        golds: List of Extraction dicts (one per instance), aligned with predictions.\n147\t\n148\t    Returns:\n149\t        Dict with keys \"precision\", \"recall\", \"f1\".\n150\t    \"\"\"\n151\t    total_tp = total_fp = total_fn = 0\n152\t    for pred, gold in zip(predictions, golds):\n153\t        tp, fp, fn = argument_match(\n154\t            pred.get(\"events\", []),\n155\t            gold.get(\"events\", []),\n156\t        )\n157\t        total_tp += tp\n158\t        total_fp += fp\n159\t        total_fn += fn\n160\t    return _prf(total_tp, total_fp, total_fn)\n161\t\n162\t\n163\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n164\t# Per-instance F1\n165\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n166\t\n167\tdef per_instance_f1(\n168\t    pred: dict,\n169\t    gold: dict,\n170\t    subtask: str = \"ner\",\n171\t) -> float:\n172\t    \"\"\"Compute F1 for a single instance.\n173\t\n174\t    Args:\n175\t        pred: Predicted Extraction dict.\n176\t        gold: Gold Extraction dict.\n177\t        subtask: \"ner\" for entity matching, \"eae\" for argument matching.\n178\t\n179\t    Returns:\n180\t        F1 score (float in [0, 1]).\n181\t    \"\"\"\n182\t    if subtask == \"ner\":\n183\t        tp, fp, fn = entity_strict_match(\n184\t            pred.get(\"entities\", []),\n185\t            gold.get(\"entities\", []),\n186\t        )\n187\t    elif subtask == \"re\":\n188\t        tp, fp, fn = relation_strict_match(\n189\t            pred.get(\"relations\", []),\n190\t            gold.get(\"relations\", []),\n191\t        )\n192\t    elif subtask == \"eae\":\n193\t        tp, fp, fn = argument_match(\n194\t            pred.get(\"events\", []),\n195\t            gold.get(\"events\", []),\n196\t        )\n197\t    else:\n198\t        raise ValueError(f\"subtask must be 'ner', 're', or 'eae', got '{subtask}'\")\n199\t    return _prf(tp, fp, fn)[\"f1\"]\n200\t\n201\t\n202\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n203\t# Per-sample F1 distribution\n204\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n205\t\n206\tdef compute_sample_f1_distribution(\n207\t    sampled_instances: list[dict],\n208\t    subtask: str = \"ner\",\n209\t) -> dict:\n210\t    \"\"\"Compute per-sample F1 distribution statistics.\n211\t\n212\t    For each instance, compute F1 of each of its N samples against gold.\n213\t    Aggregate into distribution statistics.\n214\t\n215\t    Args:\n216\t        sampled_instances: List of SampledInstance dicts, each containing\n217\t            \"gold\" (Extraction) and \"samples\" (list of Extraction).\n218\t        subtask: \"ner\" or \"eae\".\n219\t\n220\t    Returns:\n221\t        Dict with keys:\n222\t            - \"all_sample_f1s\": flat list of all per-sample F1 values\n223\t            - \"mean\": mean F1 across all samples\n224\t            - \"std\": std of F1\n225\t            - \"pct_f1_zero\": percentage of samples with F1=0.0\n226\t            - \"per_instance\": list of dicts, each with {\"mean\", \"std\", \"pct_f1_zero\", \"f1s\"}\n227\t    \"\"\"\n228\t    all_sample_f1s: list[float] = []\n229\t    per_instance: list[dict] = []\n230\t\n231\t    for inst in sampled_instances:\n232\t        gold = inst[\"gold\"]\n233\t        samples = inst.get(\"samples\", [])\n234\t        f1s = [per_instance_f1(sample, gold, subtask) for sample in samples]\n235\t        all_sample_f1s.extend(f1s)\n236\t\n237\t        if f1s:\n238\t            n_zero = sum(1 for f in f1s if f == 0.0)\n239\t            per_instance.append({\n240\t                \"mean\": statistics.mean(f1s),\n241\t                \"std\": statistics.pstdev(f1s),\n242\t                \"pct_f1_zero\": 100.0 * n_zero / len(f1s),\n243\t                \"f1s\": f1s,\n244\t            })\n245\t        else:\n246\t            per_instance.append({\"mean\": 0.0, \"std\": 0.0, \"pct_f1_zero\": 100.0, \"f1s\": []})\n247\t\n248\t    if all_sample_f1s:\n249\t        n_zero_total = sum(1 for f in all_sample_f1s if f == 0.0)\n250\t        mean = statistics.mean(all_sample_f1s)\n251\t        std = statistics.pstdev(all_sample_f1s)\n252\t        pct_f1_zero = 100.0 * n_zero_total / len(all_sample_f1s)\n253\t    else:\n254\t        mean = 0.0\n255\t        std = 0.0\n256\t        pct_f1_zero = 100.0\n257\t\n258\t    return {\n259\t        \"all_sample_f1s\": all_sample_f1s,\n260\t        \"mean\": mean,\n261\t        \"std\": std,\n262\t        \"pct_f1_zero\": pct_f1_zero,\n263\t        \"per_instance\": per_instance,\n264\t    }\n265\t\n266\t\n267\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n268\t# Correlation\n269\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n270\t\n271\tdef spearman_correlation(\n272\t    scores_a: list[float],\n273\t    scores_b: list[float],\n274\t) -> tuple[float, float]:\n275\t    \"\"\"Compute Spearman rank correlation between two score lists.\n276\t\n277\t    Args:\n278\t        scores_a: First list of scores.\n279\t        scores_b: Second list of scores (same length as scores_a).\n280\t\n281\t    Returns:\n282\t        (rho, p_value).\n283\t    \"\"\"\n284\t    if len(scores_a) != len(scores_b):\n285\t        raise ValueError(\n286\t            f\"Score lists must have equal length, got {len(scores_a)} vs {len(scores_b)}\"\n287\t        )\n288\t    if len(scores_a) < 3:\n289\t        return (0.0, 1.0)\n290\t    result = spearmanr(scores_a, scores_b)\n291\t    return (float(result.statistic), float(result.pvalue))\n292\t\n293\t\n294\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n295\t# Summary report\n296\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n297\t\n298\tdef generate_evaluation_report(\n299\t    sampled_instances: list[dict],\n300\t    consistency_scores: dict[str, list[float]],\n301\t    subtask: str = \"ner\",\n302\t) -> dict[str, Any]:\n303\t    \"\"\"Generate a structured evaluation report.\n304\t\n305\t    Computes greedy F1, oracle best-of-N F1, and consistency-F1 correlation\n306\t    for each consistency scoring method.\n307\t\n308\t    Args:\n309\t        sampled_instances: List of SampledInstance dicts, each containing\n310\t            \"id\", \"text\", \"gold\" (Extraction), \"samples\" (list of Extraction),\n311\t            and optionally \"greedy\" (Extraction).\n312\t        consistency_scores: Dict mapping method name to a list of per-instance\n313\t            consistency scores (aligned with sampled_instances).\n314\t        subtask: \"ner\" or \"eae\".\n315\t\n316\t    Returns:\n317\t        Dict with keys:\n318\t            - \"greedy_f1\": float, micro-averaged F1 of greedy outputs.\n319\t            - \"oracle_best_of_n_f1\": float, micro-averaged F1 using the\n320\t              best sample per instance.\n321\t            - \"per_instance_greedy_f1\": list of per-instance greedy F1 values.\n322\t            - \"correlations\": dict mapping method name to {\"rho\": float, \"p_value\": float}.\n323\t            - \"num_instances\": int.\n324\t            - \"num_samples_per_instance\": float, average number of samples.\n325\t    \"\"\"\n326\t    greedy_preds = []\n327\t    greedy_golds = []\n328\t    oracle_preds = []\n329\t    oracle_golds = []\n330\t    instance_greedy_f1s: list[float] = []\n331\t\n332\t    for inst in sampled_instances:\n333\t        gold = inst[\"gold\"]\n334\t\n335\t        # Greedy F1\n336\t        greedy = inst.get(\"greedy\")\n337\t        if greedy is not None:\n338\t            greedy_preds.append(greedy)\n339\t            greedy_golds.append(gold)\n340\t            instance_greedy_f1s.append(per_instance_f1(greedy, gold, subtask))\n341\t        else:\n342\t            instance_greedy_f1s.append(0.0)\n343\t\n344\t        # Oracle best-of-N: pick the sample with highest per-instance F1\n345\t        samples = inst.get(\"samples\", [])\n346\t        if samples:\n347\t            best_sample = max(samples, key=lambda s: per_instance_f1(s, gold, subtask))\n348\t            oracle_preds.append(best_sample)\n349\t            oracle_golds.append(gold)\n350\t\n351\t    # Micro-averaged scores\n352\t    f1_fn = {\"ner\": compute_ner_f1, \"re\": compute_re_f1, \"eae\": compute_eae_f1}[subtask]\n353\t    greedy_metrics = f1_fn(greedy_preds, greedy_golds) if greedy_preds else _prf(0, 0, 0)\n354\t    oracle_metrics = f1_fn(oracle_preds, oracle_golds) if oracle_preds else _prf(0, 0, 0)\n355\t\n356\t    # Correlation between consistency scores and per-instance greedy F1\n357\t    correlations: dict[str, dict[str, float]] = {}\n358\t    for method_name, scores in consistency_scores.items():\n359\t        rho, p_value = spearman_correlation(scores, instance_greedy_f1s)\n360\t        correlations[method_name] = {\"rho\": rho, \"p_value\": p_value}\n361\t\n362\t    total_samples = sum(len(inst.get(\"samples\", [])) for inst in sampled_instances)\n363\t    n = len(sampled_instances)\n364\t\n365\t    return {\n366\t        \"greedy_f1\": greedy_metrics[\"f1\"],\n367\t        \"oracle_best_of_n_f1\": oracle_metrics[\"f1\"],\n368\t        \"per_instance_greedy_f1\": instance_greedy_f1s,\n369\t        \"correlations\": correlations,\n370\t        \"num_instances\": n,\n371\t        \"num_samples_per_instance\": total_samples / n if n > 0 else 0.0,\n372\t    }\n373\t\n374\t\n375\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n376\t# Internal helpers\n377\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n378\t\n379\tdef _prf(tp: int, fp: int, fn: int) -> dict[str, float]:\n380\t    \"\"\"Compute precision, recall, F1 from raw counts.\"\"\"\n381\t    precision = tp / (tp + fp) if (tp + fp) > 0 else 0.0\n382\t    recall = tp / (tp + fn) if (tp + fn) > 0 else 0.0\n383\t    f1 = 2 * precision * recall / (precision + recall) if (precision + recall) > 0 else 0.0\n384\t    return {\"precision\": precision, \"recall\": recall, \"f1\": f1}\n385\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01HKfzCDwhxMENhz8xdBgfGN","session_id":"37f786ee-7832-4fe8-ada0-13058d333aba","uuid":"8b6835c1-75e0-4c9d-8cf0-40b89e8f514e","timestamp":"2026-05-14T10:23:03.965Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UE9qiweS8uHBqScW5vDAZs","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": false, \\\"data\\\": {}, \\\"error\\\": \\\"No literature_map.yaml found for 'struct_self_consist_ie'.\\\", \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0167Y42ihqJcnBJuj2T61bym","session_id":"37f786ee-7832-4fe8-ada0-13058d333aba","uuid":"08930a9d-a269-409d-91e3-f8072e14a271","timestamp":"2026-05-14T10:23:03.719Z"}
{"type":"system","subtype":"task_progress","task_id":"a2059b4ae02bc538c","tool_use_id":"toolu_0167Y42ihqJcnBJuj2T61bym","description":"R2: Novelty + Related Work review","usage":{"total_tokens":17426,"tool_uses":4,"duration_ms":15763},"last_tool_name":"mcp__agent-ml-research__read_project_file","uuid":"3e0c0b79-1a87-4256-b242-0f3367de7f0b","session_id":"37f786ee-7832-4fe8-ada0-13058d333aba"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01QWeXPMuHRjUBqXrbzqRA8o","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017p79ntErLamgc88oFvszbh","name":"mcp__agent-ml-research__read_project_file","input":{"project":"struct_self_consist_ie","file":"paper_framing.md","max_chars":0},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1858,"cache_read_input_tokens":15553,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1858,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0167Y42ihqJcnBJuj2T61bym","session_id":"37f786ee-7832-4fe8-ada0-13058d333aba","uuid":"c502ea1a-6d7e-4f66-84da-62368ecd1442"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017p79ntErLamgc88oFvszbh","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/paper_framing.md\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# Paper Framing — struct_self_consist_ie\\\\n\\\\n## Target Venue\\\\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (via ARR May 2026)\\\\n- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\\\\n- Deadline: ARR May cycle, 2026-05-25\\\\n\\\\n## Core Claims (2 条)\\\\n\\\\n### Claim 1 (Positive — NER)\\\\nFor entity-level information extraction, structural self-consistency (soft Jaccard over structured outputs) provides a significantly stronger confidence signal than surface agreement (Fleiss' Kappa), enabling effective test-time scaling through consistency-based sample selection.\\\\n\\\\n**MVP evidence**: NER rho_sj=0.388 (below 0.40 threshold but statistically significant advantage over FK: +12pp, p=2e-20), oracle headroom +5.5pp. N=16 (exp-001) may push rho past 0.40; if not, the 0.388 vs FK's 0.322 gap with p=2e-20 is the stronger argument.\\\\n\\\\n### Claim 2 (Diagnostic — RE + boundary condition)\\\\nThe effectiveness of consistency-based confidence is governed by task structural complexity: compound error propagation in relational tasks fundamentally degrades the consistency-accuracy correlation on the full instance set, but the signal remains valid within the model's capability range (conditional instances). This establishes a principled boundary for when structural consistency works as a TTS signal.\\\\n\\\\n**MVP evidence**: RE full rho_sj=0.234 (FAIL), RE cond rho_sj=0.372 (SJ>FK +11.8pp). Component decomposition (E1) shows all RE components equally weak (head_sj rho=0.210), ruling out metric design as cause. T=0.7 naturally separates knowledge-gap vs uncertainty errors.\\\\n\\\\n## Story Spine\\\\n\\\\n**Problem**: Test-time scaling (TTS) through sampling + selection requires a reliable confidence signal. Self-consistency has shown promise in reasoning tasks (majority voting), but structured prediction (IE) poses unique challenges: outputs have internal structure (entities, relations, triplets), and simple surface agreement ignores structural similarity.\\\\n\\\\n**Existing approaches & gaps**: Self-consistency in LLM reasoning uses exact-match voting on final answers. For structured prediction, no systematic study exists on whether structural similarity between sampled outputs correlates with accuracy. Fleiss' Kappa measures surface agreement but treats structured outputs as flat tokens, missing structural information.\\\\n\\\\n**Our framing**: We introduce structural self-consistency (soft Jaccard) as a confidence signal for IE test-time scaling. Unlike prior work on reasoning self-consistency, we operate on structured outputs where the metric choice fundamentally matters. We discover a task-complexity boundary: structural consistency is a strong signal for entity-level tasks (NER) where errors are independent, but degrades for relational tasks (RE) where compound error propagation across head/tail/type components amplifies noise. This diagnostic finding provides practical guidance on when TTS works for structured prediction.\\\\n\\\\n**Headline result template**: \\\\\\\"On SciERC NER, structural self-consistency achieves rho=0.39 correlation with accuracy (vs rho=0.32 for Fleiss' Kappa, p<1e-19), enabling +X F1 improvement through best-of-N selection. However, on relation extraction, full-set correlation drops to rho=0.23 due to compound error propagation — though conditional analysis (within-capability instances) recovers rho=0.37 with SJ>FK by 12pp.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\\\\n\\\\n### R1: \\\\\\\"Only one NER dataset — generalization unclear\\\\\\\"\\\\n- **Mitigation**: exp-002 (CoNLL-2003) + exp-003 (OntoNotes) validate cross-dataset\\\\n- **Priority**: P0, must address before submission\\\\n\\\\n### R2: \\\\\\\"Only one model family (Qwen3-8B)\\\\\\\"\\\\n- **Mitigation**: exp-007 (LLaMA-3.1-8B or similar) shows model-agnostic effect\\\\n- **Priority**: P1, strongly recommended\\\\n\\\\n### R3: \\\\\\\"RE negative result makes the contribution narrow\\\\\\\"\\\\n- **Mitigation**: Frame Claim 2 as diagnostic contribution — identifying WHY and WHEN consistency fails is as valuable as showing it works. Component decomposition + temperature sensitivity provide mechanistic explanation.\\\\n- **Priority**: Addressed by framing, reinforced by exp-004 (RE diagnostic analysis)\\\\n\\\\n### R4: \\\\\\\"No actual TTS improvement demonstrated\\\\\\\"\\\\n- **Mitigation**: exp-006 (adaptive compute demo) shows concrete F1 gains from SJ-based selection vs random vs FK\\\\n- **Priority**: P1, high impact\\\\n\\\\n### R5: \\\\\\\"Sample size N=8 may be too small for reliable SJ estimation\\\\\\\"\\\\n- **Mitigation**: exp-001 (N=16) tests scaling effect on NER; if rho improves, demonstrates N-sensitivity\\\\n- **Priority**: P0\\\\n\\\\n### R6: \\\\\\\"Conditional analysis cherry-picks favorable instances\\\\\\\"\\\\n- **Mitigation**: All-zero instances represent fundamental knowledge gaps (model consistently fails), not borderline cases. The separation is principled: consistency should measure uncertainty, not inability. Temperature analysis (T=0.7 increases all-zero count while improving conditional rho) supports this interpretation.\\\\n- **Priority**: Addressed by analysis in paper\\\\n\\\\n## Venue Fit\\\\n\\\\nEMNLP is well-suited for:\\\\n- NLP-focused analysis of IE methods\\\\n- Empirical studies with diagnostic findings\\\\n- Negative results that provide principled explanations\\\\n\\\\nRisk: purely analytical paper without a new method. Mitigation: structural self-consistency + the diagnostic framework ARE the methodological contributions; the findings provide actionable guidelines.\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 5246, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0167Y42ihqJcnBJuj2T61bym","session_id":"37f786ee-7832-4fe8-ada0-13058d333aba","uuid":"3543be73-ef35-4bf8-8883-53bd157ddce6","timestamp":"2026-05-14T10:23:04.160Z"}
